        "original_id": "94352f90-50b3-5185-a68a-bf7249062c70",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Heaney, Franklin D. Roosevelt\n- Organizations: Works Progress Administration\n- Places: Mount Hood, Timberline Lodge, Clackamas County, Government Camp\n- Roads: Oregon Route 173, U.S. Route 26\n- Topics: Great Depression\n\nFacts:\n- During the Great Depression in the 1930s, Charles Heaney worked as an artist for the Works Progress Administration and created several works featuring Mount Hood and Timberline Lodge.\n- On September 28, 1937, President Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicated Timberline Lodge.\n- Oregon Route 173 is an Oregon state highway that runs from Timberline Lodge in Clackamas County to U.S. Route 26 near Government Camp.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
